  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;BURGESS COMPANY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Burgess Company was an American company that designed and built the Burgess Type O Gunbus at Marblehead, Massachusetts."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARBLEHEAD, MASSACHUSETTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marblehead, Massachusetts is the location where the Burgess Type O Gunbus was built."&lt;SEP&gt;"Marblehead, Massachusetts is the location where the Burgess Type O Gunbuses were built."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH ADMIRALTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British Admiralty is the department responsible for the command and management of the Royal Navy and ordered 36 Burgess Type O Gunbuses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROYAL NAVAL AIR SERVICE (RNAS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Royal Naval Air Service (RNAS) is the branch of the British Armed Forces responsible for naval aviation and was intended to use the Burgess Type O Gunbuses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HENDON AERODROME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hendon Aerodrome is the location where the first Burgess Type O Gunbus was flown and some were used for training."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EASTCHURCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eastchurch is a location where some of the Burgess Type O Gunbuses were used for training."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eastchurch is another location where some of the Burgess Type O Gunbuses were used for training."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STURTEVANT ENGINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Sturtevant engine is a 140 hp (104 kW) engine that powered the Burgess Type O Gunbuses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIR JOHN ERSKINE, 23RD EARL OF MAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sir John Erskine, 23rd Earl of Mar is a historical figure mentioned in the context of the British Wars."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOBBIN JOCK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ROLE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bobbin Jock is a disparaging nickname for Sir John Erskine, 23rd Earl of Mar, mentioned in the context of the British Wars."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VICKERS, SON &amp; MAXIM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vickers, Son &amp; Maxim is an armaments contractor that was contracted by the Admiralty to produce military equipment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADMIRALTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Admiralty is the department responsible for the command and management of the Royal Navy and placed an order with Vickers, Son &amp; Maxim."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRITISH WARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The British Wars refer to a series of conflicts involving Britain, including the one in which Sir John Erskine, 23rd Earl of Mar, played a role."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WWI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WWI, or World War I, is a major global conflict in which Britain was involved, and during which there was a feverish spy mania."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WORLD WAR I (WWI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"World War I (WWI) is a major global conflict in which Britain was involved, and during which there was a feverish spy mania."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1915&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1915 is the year when the British Admiralty ordered 36 Burgess Type O Gunbuses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1912&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1912 is the year when the Admiralty placed an order with Vickers, Son &amp; Maxim."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1715&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1715 is the year mentioned in the context of the British Wars."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;1732&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DATE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"1732 is the year of death for Sir John Erskine, 23rd Earl of Mar."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;140 HP (104 KW)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MEASUREMENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"140 hp (104 kW) is the power rating of the Sturtevant engine that powered the Burgess Type O Gunbuses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;36&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUMBER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"36 is the number of Burgess Type O Gunbuses ordered by the British Admiralty."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;36 TYPE OS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MODEL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"36 Type Os is the model designation of the Burgess Type O Gunbuses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RNAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RNAS is the abbreviation for the Royal Naval Air Service, which was intended to use the Burgess Type O Gunbuses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HENDON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hendon is part of Hendon Aerodrome, where the first Burgess Type O Gunbus was flown and some were used for training."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STURTEVANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sturtevant is the manufacturer of the engine that powered the Burgess Type O Gunbuses."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0087-b8c4b9b28a48</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BURGESS TYPE O GUNBUS&quot;">
